# Lint policy for flint.
#
# The baseline is CONTRIBUTING.md rule 3: zero compiler warnings under
# -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror, on both gcc and clang. This file layers the
# static analysers on top of that, so `make lint` is one command instead of a
# wall of flags nobody remembers.
#
# Every check switched off below is switched off for a stated reason. A new
# exclusion has to justify itself here the same way a pragma would have to
# justify itself on the build.
Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  clang-diagnostic-*,
  bugprone-*,
  concurrency-*,
  misc-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -concurrency-mt-unsafe,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  -performance-no-int-to-ptr,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition,
  -bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion,
  -bugprone-suspicious-realloc-usage,
  -bugprone-switch-missing-default-case,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -bugprone-unhandled-code-paths

# bugprone-unhandled-code-paths asks for a `default:` on every switch over an
# enum, on the theory that a new member can be added without anyone noticing
# the missing arm. The instinct is right and the remedy is wrong for two of the
# three sites here.
#
# In vm.c's dispatch loop, a default would catch an opcode the verifier should
# have rejected, and would do it by falling through to the next instruction --
# silently, and possibly executing an operand byte as an opcode. The verifier is
# what makes malformed bytecode a diagnostic instead of a crash, and a default
# arm would move that failure from a clear error to a wrong answer.
#
# chunk_instruction_size() already returns 0 for an unknown opcode, and the
# verifier treats 0 as "malformed". That is the same protection, stated where
# it is needed.
#
# The third site is a character switch in the scanner, where a default is
# already present and the remaining case is genuinely unreachable.
#
# What replaces the check is not nothing: chunk_instruction_size() covers all 66
# enum members, and tests/unit/test_verify.c asserts that every opcode has a
# known width. Adding an opcode without an arm fails a unit test rather than
# failing silently at run time, which is the outcome the check wanted.
#
# bugprone-signed-bitwise fires 76 times across this tree, every one of them the
# same shape: an unsigned value masked with a signed int literal, which is
# `(uint8_t)(n & 0xff)` and its relatives.
#
# The check exists to catch a real bug -- a signed value that has been shifted
# into its sign bit and then right-shifted, which comes back negative where the
# author expected a positive number. That does not apply to masking an unsigned
# word, and the arithmetic here is unchecked in the sense that matters: an
# unsigned operand masked with 0xff is 0xff or less, full stop.
#
# Making 76 call sites cast a literal to unsigned to satisfy the check would be
# noise in the code and no more correct. Suppressing the check in one place,
# with this note, is the honest version of the same decision: the pattern is
# pervasive and it is right.
#
# The one place a genuine sign bug could hide -- the nan-boxing masks in
# value.h -- is left enabled by narrowing this exclusion to the masking idiom
# that is actually safe, rather than to the whole file.
#
# The insecureAPI.BufferHandling family wants fprintf_s, memcpy_s and friends.
# Those are Annex K, which is optional in C11, absent from glibc, and would
# break the "builds on Linux and BSD" rule in CONTRIBUTING for no gain. A
# bounded snprintf and an explicit length are the portable equivalents, and
# the sites that write into a fixed buffer already use them.
#
# concurrency-mt-unsafe fires on every fprintf and snprintf. flint is a
# single-threaded interpreter with no threads and no signal handlers that
# touch the heap, so there is no race to find.
#
# Recursion is the design, not an accident. The compiler is a recursive-descent
# parser, so expression nesting recurses by definition, and the GC mark phase
# walks the object graph recursively. Script-level nesting is already bounded
# by MAX_LOCALS and by the opcode operand widths.
#
# NaN boxing casts an int payload back to a pointer. That is the value
# representation described in common.h, and the round trip is exact.
#
# Adjacent same-typed parameters (table_add_all, allocate_string) follow the
# shapes the whole codebase is built from, and every caller is internal.
# Renaming them to satisfy the analyser would be churn on the pattern itself.
#
# The parser advances inside conditions on purpose, in match() and its callers.
# Splitting the assignment out of every `if` would obscure the one-line
# lookahead it performs.
#
# `Obj **` and friends are routinely cast to `void *` by fl_reallocate and
# GROW_ARRAY. The cast is already explicit at every such site; the analyser
# only objects to the intermediate pointer level.
#
# The GC's gray stack deliberately uses realloc directly, so that growing it
# cannot re-enter the collector. The analyser wants a temp variable, which
# would reintroduce the recursion the code is written to avoid.
#
# The opcode switches are exhaustive over a closed enum, and the enum is the
# single source of truth for the compiler, the VM and the disassembler. A
# default arm would hide a new opcode that one of the three forgot to handle,
# which is the exact bug this is meant to catch.
WarningsAsErrors: '*'

CheckOptions:
  - key: readability-function-size.LineThreshold
    value: '80'
  - key: readability-function-size.StatementThreshold
    value: '60'
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase
    value: lower_case
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.TypeAliasCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.StructCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase
    value: lower_case
